      "message": "@francois.gaffie@ampere.cars Francois, I have realized there is a problem with this moving of files. There are car devices like `seahawk` that already have targets with same names for their vendor configuration. Now as `libaudiopolicyengineconfigurable` start depending on these prebuilts from system, both these new modules and the existing vendor modules end up in the device makefile, causing a name conflict. And we can\u0027t use `soong_namespace` to isolate them because we actually need both. That\u0027s because since the framework must support both HIDL and AIDL HAL, we have to always have these new config files in `/system/etc`, regardless of which HAL the device uses.\n\nI\u0027ve attempted to rename these `prebuilt_etc` targets to give them `Sys` prefix, but then I\u0027ve got a bit confused because there are many similar prebuilts across different directories here. Could you please help with this?",
